Patch 3004: cellAudio WASAPI backend re-opens the default render device when the device is lost or the default changes.

Symptom (J-Stars tester, after alt-tab): the sound was gone for the rest of the run. The backend opened the endpoint once.
When GetCurrentPadding then failed (AUDCLNT_E_DEVICE_INVALIDATED on a default-device change, a device taken by another
program, sleep, an audio service restart) audio_backend_room returned -1 and the mix thread paced on the clock with no
output until exit. The submit path also ignored the HRESULTs of GetCurrentPadding, GetBuffer and ReleaseBuffer.

Now: a result that means the device is gone (padding failure, or DEVICE_INVALIDATED / SERVICE_NOT_RUNNING /
RESOURCES_INVALIDATED / ENDPOINT_CREATE_FAILED from GetBuffer or ReleaseBuffer) releases client, render client and event
and starts re-opening the current default render endpoint with the same format negotiation as the first open (48 kHz
stereo float, event callback, autoconvert; the fallback without event now uses a fresh client). Opening runs on its own
thread so the mix thread never waits for Activate/Initialize; the first try is at the loss, then every 0.5, 1, 2, 2 ... s.
Meanwhile mixing and the guest-side pacing are unchanged (the mix thread paces on the performance counter, as with no
device). A start with no device now also retries. Once a second, while healthy, the default endpoint id is compared with
the one the stream plays on: a stream on the old device keeps playing there after the user switches, so no HRESULT
reports it; a change triggers the same re-open. Log: one "[cellAudio] audio device lost (0x... in ...)" line per loss, up
to three "re-open try N failed" lines, one "audio device re-opened after N ms" line.

The decision logic (which HRESULTs mean re-open, retry timing, endpoint-id comparison) is in audio_wasapi_recover.h with
no Windows dependency; libs/audio/tests/test_audio_device_recover.c drives it with fake HRESULTs and a fake clock.
Upstream candidate (general fix, no J-Stars specifics). Not run in a game: cellAudio.c compiled (mingw -Wall -Wextra) and the host test run; the full exe not built yet.

